## Stack-Specific Patterns & Traps
- **TypeScript**: Use `===` for all comparisons (never loose equality). The codebase type-checks with tsc; verify the types match.
- **vitest**: Run tests with `npm test` within the target codeline. Tests live near source files with `.test.ts` or `.spec.ts` suffixes. Before fixing, read the actual test file to verify what edge cases it covers—do not trust comments or AC text alone.
- **Boundary conditions**: For fare rules and schedules, verify off-by-one errors in comparisons (`>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=`) and loop bounds. Investigators in the roles (mocka-fares-investigator and mockb-schedule-investigator) verify the exact operator and indices before the implementer (fare-boundary-engineer or departure-board-engineer) commits.
- **Scope isolation**: MOCK3-1 fixes are confined to mocka. MOCK3-2 fixes are confined to mockb. Do not refactor across codelines.
